        "title": "Rephrase cloud resource limit file recovery instructions",
        "summary": "The constant `CLOUD_RESOURCE_FILES_WHERE` in the desktop-cloud shared module now tells web clients to open the same chat in the Desktop app and choose Local to continue, rather than merely stating that only Desktop can recover the files. The comment above the constant attributes the change to a 2026-10-28 finding that the previous wording led web users to start a new, empty Cloud chat instead of resuming from the saved copy. The `cloudResourceExplanation` function already routed this sentence into the `movesLocally` false branch, so no call-site logic changed and only the displayed text updates.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "The diff in `common/src/desktop-cloud/resource-limits.ts` rewrites the literal string value of `CLOUD_RESOURCE_FILES_WHERE`, and the accompanying test hunk in `common/src/desktop-cloud/resource-limits.test.ts` asserts the new sentence appears in the `movesLocally: false` branch of `cloudResourceExplanation`.",
